# The Monitor console - frontend server settings.
#
# Copy to .env (which is gitignored) and fill in. Every value here is optional;
# the defaults below are what the server uses if the variable is absent.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing in this file is read by the browser directly. The server hands the
# console only what GET /api/config chooses to expose, at request time - so no
# secret ever ends up inside a file under static/.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the Monitor API (phase1/phase2/phase3 routes) is listening. The browser
# never sees this host: every /api/* call is proxied through this server, which
# is why the console has no CORS configuration at all.
BACKEND_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Maps
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Browser key for the Maps JavaScript API.
#
# THIS KEY IS PUBLIC BY NATURE. It is served to the page and any visitor can
# read it out of the network tab - that is how the Maps JS API works, and no
# amount of obfuscation changes it. The only real control is a restriction:
#
#   Google Cloud console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials -> (this key)
#     * Application restrictions: HTTP referrers (web sites)
#       add exactly the origins that serve the console, e.g.
#         http://127.0.0.1:8080/*
#         http://localhost:8080/*
#         https://your-console-host/*
#     * API restrictions: restrict to "Maps JavaScript API" only.
#
# Set the referrer restriction BEFORE putting the key here. An unrestricted key
# is billable by anyone who copies it.
#
# Leave empty and the console degrades gracefully: /api/config returns
# maps_key: null and the map panel draws its SVG vicinity fallback instead.
GOOGLE_MAPS_BROWSER_KEY=

# Cloud-styled Map IDs, one per theme, so the basemap follows the console's
# light/dark toggle. Optional - without them the map renders in the default
# Google style. Create them under Google Maps Platform -> Map Management.
GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID_LIGHT=
GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID_DARK=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Bind address and port for the console. 127.0.0.1 keeps it local-only; use
# 0.0.0.0 only behind something that terminates TLS and enforces auth.
FRONTEND_HOST=127.0.0.1
FRONTEND_PORT=8080

# Upstream timeout, in seconds, for proxied /api/* calls.
#
# Deliberately generous. A bundle read on the backend can trigger a live Mireye
# fetch, which is billed and can take tens of seconds. A short client timeout
# does NOT cancel the server-side work - the backend keeps fetching and keeps
# billing, we just stop listening and throw away a result we already paid for.
# Raise this rather than lower it.
PROXY_TIMEOUT_S=40.0
